From fe8f81869fb4b54a34ba9926155f7dace92b27dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bsp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 07:58:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 41/49] moe cache: copy-back ahead in a decode take-over waits
 on the compute stream only for slots of unknown fill state
 (GGML_MOE_FILL_FENCE)

precopy_plan_locked recorded pol_ev on the compute stream for the side stream's wait whenever it issued copies: one
more marker packet per policy call (FINDINGS 745).  Each arena slot now knows when its last fill landed (slot_seq: 0 for
the synchronous seeds, the committing take-over's lag-flag value for a deferred fill, -1 otherwise).  Inside a decode
take-over a candidate whose fill the flag shows landed is copied without a wait, one filled in this take-over or not
landed yet is left for a later call, and pol_ev is recorded (once) only before a copy of a slot of unknown state.
Outside a take-over and with GGML_MOE_FILL_FENCE=0 every copy waits as before.
